        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Death Gasp"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nThe shadern draws in a deep breath and holds it, temporarily suspending their biological processes and becoming undead. The shadern gains the undead trait and becomes immune to bleed, death effects, disease, paralyzed, poison, and sleep. Any such effects the shadern is currently inflicted with are suspended but take effect again once they take a breath.\n\nDeath Gasp lasts as long as the shadern holds their breath (up to 8 rounds; Core Rulebook 478)."
            },
            "action_type": {
              "value": "none"
            },
            "action_cost": {
              "value": "one_action"
            },
            "action_attack_bonus": {
              "value": 0
            },
            "action_damage_variants": {
              "value": []
            },
            "id": "cdb75b3f-5657-431e-8cb9-bee0cc097bc1",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:53.849899"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Exhale"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(divine, evocation, fire)\n\nThe shadern exhales a cloud of thick smoke in a 10-foot burst centered on them. The cloud remains in place for 1d4 rounds. All creatures within the smoke become concealed, and all creatures outside the smoke become concealed to creatures within it. Exhaling ends Death Gasp, as the shadern ceases holding their breath."
            },
